description:
Problem (parity audit 2026-10-26): the local review re-implements plan building, the soundness predicate, the classification fallback, the decision mapping (it clears any Medium/Low-only SHIP WITH FIXES and ignores the max_defects rule that forces DO NOT SHIP in CI), the patch digest (raw bytes, incomparable with CI), the cache and the display. It runs the branch's own reviewer code, OMP config and inert-paths; never runs the disk scan; uses one machine-global lock; is blind to prior reviews, carried defects and disputes even when the PR already exists; pushes the branch ref, not the reviewed SHA. local.py:187 hard-codes no disputes.

Outcome: make pr-open invokes the same driver as CI with a local adapter, executed from a cached export of origin/develop's reviewer package (owner Q11 interim):
- change source: the git merge-base diff;
- PR context: none before the PR exists; read-only GitHub history (prior reviews, carried defects, disputes) once it does;
- classification: TypeSafe key from the keychain or environment; without it the review pends, cannot run, and pr-open refuses (owner Q3 with #8);
- credentials: oracle-local or oracle-cloud;
- harness: the pinned, verified cache binary;
- disk scan with local roots, including the gateway token directory; redaction also covers TS_AUTHKEY and the host's gateway token values when present;
- lock scope unchanged (one review per machine); the wait message names the holder's branch and start time;
- cache keyed by the digest defined by oracle-carry-byte-identical-20261026, base, a hash of all trusted inputs (including the soundness manifest), the harness version and the gateway model mapping; the cache location is fixed per user, with no environment override (BENCHBOX_LOCAL_ORACLE_DIR removed); a same-user process can still forge cache files, so CI remains the control;
- a quota absence persists pool_blocked_until locally so that pool waits for its reset;
- the shared finalize and judge decide; pr-open blocks on Critical or High findings or a DO NOT SHIP decision from that shared judgement (owner Q1). The override line stays only until oracle-local-findings-record-disputes-20261026 replaces it;
- pr-open pushes exactly the reviewed SHA and arms that SHA.
Delete local.py's parallel plan builder, soundness predicate, classify fork, _result mapping and raw digest; local.py keeps adapter code only.

Decision gates:
1. Before merging the pend-without-key behaviour, confirm the owner's keychain entry exists (security find-generic-password -s TYPESAFE_API_KEY exits 0; never print the value). If absent, set this item blocked with the owner step security add-generic-password -s TYPESAFE_API_KEY -a "$USER" -w and continue other items.
2. Keep the classifier key out of the reviewer's process tree exactly as CI does; prove with a test that inspects the environment of every ancestor of the reviewer process, not only the attempt process.
3. Parity proof: run the driver with the CI adapter and the local adapter over the same fixture repository and patch; assert identical plan (except adapter fields), identical judgement and identical block or clear mapping. Fix any difference that is not environment-forced, or stop and report it.
4. The trusted export never includes the branch's working tree; if origin/develop cannot be fetched, the review cannot run (refuse, #8).
5. Pre-merge Mac smoke: run the branch's reviewer package through a test-only option that cannot push or open a PR, since make pr-open uses develop's export.

Item guardrails: CI behaviour unchanged (the CI driver's golden tests stay green); the local review posts nothing; never use the omp on PATH.

Common guardrails: work only in a linked worktree created by make worktree-create, then make agent-write-preflight; the primary clone is read-only. Never use git stash (refs/stash is shared across worktrees). Commit as Joe Harris <joeharris76@gmail.com>, staging explicit paths only; no git add -A, no --no-verify, no SKIP, no agent trailers. Durable text (commits, PR bodies, docs, code) carries no tracker ids, session labels or plan references. Maintained code has no explanatory comments or docstrings (make comment-policy-check). Before publishing run make docs-reference-inventory-check, make doc-contracts-guard and make pr-preflight, and self-review with the code review action, fixing every Critical and Required finding. Publish only with make pr-open: never gh pr create, a raw push-and-open, or a PR-body override line; if make pr-open refuses, stop and report the exact refusal instead of routing around it. Until oracle-omp-pin-single-source-20261026 merges, make pr-open may run only with PATH prefixed by the darwin-arm64 omp 18.12.1 build recorded in that item (SHA-256 fa41b27d434380e99b713e4f9ced0f73eb1fc0c409fdf23a57c119971d24bac5, from https://build.stencil.so/d/omp/20261017-231446-291e055/omp-darwin-arm64), verified with shasum immediately before use; never any other side-loaded omp. Close out only with oracle SHIP on the exact head, every oracle thread answered (reply naming the fixing SHA, then resolve) and make pr-arm; never raw gh pr merge or a ruleset or settings change, and never a stand-in, adjudication or backoff reset unless the owner names the PR and head (and the finding) in the current request after an Owner instruction comment. Never edit, delete, dismiss or minimise an oracle review, review comment or commit status, and never post a commit status by hand. Run /oracle-review only on a pending or absent head, or after a Dispute: reply with file:line counter-evidence; never to re-roll a decided head. Do not close, reopen, rerun or rebase other PRs. Until oracle-gateway-cloud-builder-access-20261025 merges, publish only from the owner's Mac. Rollback: if a change to the verdict or gate workflows or to the local review breaks its first live run after merge in a way that blocks other PRs, stop, run make trunk-revert PR=<n>, and report to the owner, who chooses between an absence stand-in and the broken-oracle-gate procedure. Never print tokens, keys, or the gateway URL or hostname; never spend model quota outside the review harness. Owner decisions are recorded in context and in the decisions file; a step that would contradict one stops and asks the owner.
